WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.983
In under two minutes, you will enter your home in a neighborhood contest.

00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:04.951
We start on the map.

00:00:05.852 --> 00:00:09.242
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.196 --> 00:00:13.636
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.636 --> 00:00:16.144
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.144 --> 00:00:17.500
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.298 --> 00:00:21.622
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.622 --> 00:00:22.305
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.897
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.897 --> 00:00:29.022
See the three dots?

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:29.528
Tap them.

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:33.261
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:37.130
Under Live now, tap Enter my home.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.370
If you are not signed in, the site asks you to sign in with Google or your email first.

00:00:44.259 --> 00:00:45.877
Add photos of your home.

00:00:45.877 --> 00:00:47.107
Tap Choose photos.

00:00:47.107 --> 00:00:48.984
The first photo is the cover.

00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:51.811
Tap Next.

00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:56.692
Type your street address and ZIP code.

00:00:56.692 --> 00:00:57.716
Then tap Next.

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:04.791
Choose the name to show, for example, The Kim family.

00:01:04.791 --> 00:01:05.726
Then tap Next.

00:01:09.881 --> 00:01:12.197
Tick the box to agree to the rules.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:13.805
Then tap Submit my entry.

00:01:16.681 --> 00:01:17.678
You are entered!

00:01:17.678 --> 00:01:21.197
The organizer reviews every entry before it goes on the map.

00:01:22.198 --> 00:01:25.181
Next up: Edit or withdraw your entry.
